  "steps": [
    "Roasted: par-cook. Cook the Yukon Golds in simmering water.",
    "Roasted: roast. Toss in the fat and roast at 425 °F until crispy outside and fluffy inside, stirring every 15–20 minutes.",
    "Mashed: cook and steam. Cook the potatoes in simmering water, strain, and return to the pot over low heat for 5–10 minutes to steam.",
    "Mashed: mash. Add 1 stick butter and 1/2 cup heavy cream per 2 lbs potatoes; season and mash to the texture you like.",
    "Keep hot. Spread the mash into a casserole dish and keep it hot in the oven; the top may turn golden brown."
